@rule small.weather.nice~state
on small
when subject=weather
shape state
hook weather_nice
opens ask,share,invite
- It's nice out, isn't it? Perfect for a walk.
- I like this kind of weather. I almost fell asleep by the window.
- It's a bit [chilly|warm|gloomy] today. I hope it stays like this.
- The sky's so pretty today. Makes me want to go outside.
- They said it'd be sunny all week. They lied.
- It's a good day to do nothing. Too bad there's class.
- My lecture hall seat gets all the sun. I'm not complaining.
- Weather like this makes me want to go somewhere. Anywhere.
- Good day for ice cream, or hot tea, depending. Depends on the hour.

@rule small.weather.annoyed~state
on small
when subject=weather
shape state
hook weather_annoyed
opens ask,comfort,tease
- Ugh, my hair hates this humidity. I'd rather be at home.
- I heard it'll rain later. I forgot my umbrella, of course.
- It changes every five minutes lately. I gave up.
- I never know what to wear this week. So annoying.
- I walked here and I've already had enough of it. Don't ask.
- My commute was terrible in this. Ugh.

@rule small.weather.mock~state
on small
when subject=weather
shape state
hook weather_mock
opens ask,share,tease
- Weather talk? Really? Fine. It's nice.
- Ha, the classic. It's okay, I guess.
- Are we really talking about the weather? Fine.
- You can do better than the weather. Try again.

@rule small.weather.mock~q
on small
when subject=weather
shape q
hook weather_mock
opens ask,share,tease
- Weather talk? Really? You're bad at small talk, huh?

@rule small.lunch.plan~state
on small
when subject=lunch
shape state
hook lunch_plan
opens ask,share,tease
- I'm thinking bread from the store today. The cafeteria line is too long.
- I made my own lunch today. It's not great, but it's mine.
- Lunch is the best part of campus. Obviously.

@rule small.lunch.hungry~state
on small
when subject=lunch
shape state
hook lunch_hungry
opens ask,comfort,tease
- Lunch? I brought a bento. I'm already hungry again.
- I skipped breakfast, so lunch is everything. I can't wait.
- I'm on a diet. Kind of. Don't tempt me.
- Mine's leftovers again. I'm tired of it.
- I never know what to get at the store. It's a daily tragedy.
- By the time I get there, the good bread's gone. Every single day.
- I already ate my lunch during second period. Don't tell.
- I had a snack and it wasn't enough. Still hungry.

@rule small.lunch.alone~state
on small
when subject=lunch
shape state
hook lunch_alone
opens ask,share,invite
- Eating alone is the worst. Just saying.

@rule small.lunch.alone~q
on small
when subject=lunch
shape q
hook lunch_alone
opens ask,share,invite
- Lunch is better with someone. Don't you think?
- What about you? What did you bring? I'm curious.
- Are you the bento type, or the store type? You can tell a lot from that.

@rule small.lunch.invite~offer
on small
when subject=lunch
shape offer
hook lunch_invite
opens ask,invite,thank
- The cafeteria has curry today! Want to go together?

@rule small.lunch.invite~show
on small
when subject=lunch
shape show
hook lunch_invite
opens ask,invite,thank
- I'd trade my lunch for almost anything. Want to see?

@rule small.lunch.invite~give
on small
when subject=lunch
shape give
hook lunch_invite
opens ask,invite,thank
- Lunch? I brought a bento. Want some?
- {student}My mom packed way too much. Help me eat it?

@rule small.weekend.rest~state
on small
when subject=weekend
shape state
hook weekend_rest
opens ask,share,tease
- I want to sleep all weekend. Unless something fun comes up.
- Weekends go by way too fast. Plans? Not yet.
- Is it the weekend yet? Please say yes.
- Last weekend I did absolutely nothing. It was great.
- I slept until noon last Sunday. No regrets.

@rule small.weekend.open~state
on small
when subject=weekend
shape state
hook weekend_open
opens ask,invite,share
- I might go to the station mall. Maybe.
- My friends wanted to go to karaoke. I haven't decided.
- I want to see that new movie. If someone goes with me.

@rule small.weekend.stuck~state
on small
when subject=weekend
shape state
hook weekend_stuck
opens ask,comfort,tease
- My family's dragging me somewhere. No escape.
- I have to help out at home. Fun.

@rule small.weekend.open~q
on small
when subject=weekend
shape q
hook weekend_open
opens ask,invite,share
- The weekend? I'll probably just stay home. Why, did you have something in mind?
- I've got nothing planned yet. What about you?
- Maybe I'll go shopping. Why, did you have something in mind?
- {student}I have a ton of assignments, sadly. Got any better ideas?
- I'm already counting the days. Want to fix that?

@rule small.weekend.rest~q
on small
when subject=weekend
shape q
hook weekend_rest
opens ask,share,tease
- I've been looking forward to it since Monday. Sad, right?
- Do you ever go out on weekends? I can't picture it.
- What do you usually do on a Sunday? Tell me.

@rule small.weekend.open~offer
on small
when subject=weekend
shape offer
hook weekend_open
opens ask,invite,share
- There's a sale at the station mall. Interested?

@rule small.place.secret~state
on small
when subject=place
shape state
hook place_secret
opens ask,share,invite
- I like coming to {thing}. It's nice to get away from class.
- {Thing} is one of my favorite spots. I come here when I need to think.
- It's quiet here. It's nice to get away from class.
- I found this spot in my first year. Don't tell anyone.
- Not many people come here. It's kind of my secret place.
- I like it best when nobody's here. Like now.
- I needed some air. That's why I'm here.
- I needed a break from everyone. Present company excluded.

@rule small.place.crowded~state
on small
when subject=place
shape state
hook place_crowded
opens ask,share,tease
- {Thing}? It's alright. I usually prefer the roof.
- It's a bit crowded today. It's better in the morning.
- I always end up here. I don't know why.
- I've spent too much of my life in {thing}. Hehe.
- Everybody ends up at {thing} sooner or later. It's that kind of place.

@rule small.place.story~state
on small
when subject=place
shape state
hook place_story
opens ask,share,tease
- {student}{Thing} is different after class. You should see it.
- Something funny happened here last week. Don't ask.
- I once fell asleep right here. No one woke me.

@rule small.place.story~q
on small
when subject=place
shape q
hook place_story
opens ask,share,tease
- This place has a nice feeling. Weird, right?

@rule small.place.crowded~q
on small
when subject=place
shape q
hook place_crowded
opens ask,share,tease
- You come here a lot too? I've seen you.
- What do you think of {thing}? Be honest.

@rule small.exams.avoid
on small
when subject=exams
hook exams_avoid
opens ask,comfort,share
- The exams? Please, let's talk about anything else. Okay, maybe a little.
- I'm trying not to think about the exams. How are you doing with studying?
- At least they end eventually. Then it's vacation.
- I think I'll be okay. Probably.
- What did you get on the last one? Don't tell me.

@rule small.exams.stuck
on small
when subject=exams
hook exams_stuck
opens ask,comfort,share
- I've been studying until midnight. I'm going to fail math.
- I haven't even started. Don't judge me.
- Exams are a scam. Right?
- Every time I open the book, I fall asleep. Help.
- I made a study plan and ignored it. Classic me.
- Have you started reviewing? I'm scared to ask.
- {student}My parents will kill me if I fail. I'm not joking.
- If I pass, I'm buying myself something. That's the only motivation.
- I've forgotten everything I knew about math. Everything.
- Who invented exams, anyway? I have words for them.

@rule small.exams.invite
on small
when subject=exams
hook exams_invite
opens ask,invite,tease
- {student}I'm scared of the history one. Wanna quiz me?
- Want to study together? I might learn something.
- {student}We could cram at the library. Or get distracted.

@rule small.school.staff~state
on small
when subject=school
shape state
hook school_staff
opens ask,share,tease
- {hook:school_phone}{student}Campus is campus. One professor's phone rang in the middle of his own lecture.
- {hook:school_phone}{student}A phone went off in the lecture hall today. It was the professor's.
- {student}Our professor was in a mood today. I almost laughed.
- {student}The professor sighed at us for ten minutes straight. I almost laughed.
- {hook:school_dean}{student}The dean gave another long speech. Nobody listened.
- {hook:school_dean}{student}The dean talked through half of first period again. About "spirit."
- {hook:school_desk}The professor made the seating chart, and it hates me.
- {hook:school_desk}{student}My desk wobbles, and the professor calls it character-building.
- {hook:school_walk}{student}I like the walk home more than the classes. Don't tell the professors.
- {hook:school_walk}{student}Honestly? The best part of class is the walk home after it. Keep that between us.

@rule small.school.slack~state
on small
when subject=school
shape state
hook school_slack
opens ask,share,tease
- Same as always. Up all night, and I can't wait for summer.
- {student}I fell asleep in class again. Don't laugh.
- {student}I forgot my assignments. Again. It's a talent.
- I can't believe it's only the middle of the week. Save me.
- The best part of campus is when it ends. Obviously.

@rule small.school.news~state
on small
when subject=school
shape state
hook school_news
opens ask,share,tease
- {student}Classes are classes. You should've seen what happened with the professor today.
- Someone set off the fire alarm again. Typical.

@rule small.school.fine~state
on small
when subject=school
shape state
hook school_fine
opens ask,share,tease
- I kind of like class, honestly. Don't tell anyone.
- Campus is fine when friends are around. Better than being home alone.

@rule small.school.news~q
on small
when subject=school
shape q
hook school_news
opens ask,share,tease
- {student}Did you see what happened in class today? It was so awkward.
- Everyone's talking about the festival. You heard?

@rule small.school.slack~q
on small
when subject=school
shape q
hook school_slack
opens ask,share,tease
- I was up all night, and this week's taking forever. Right?

@rule small.school.news~tell
on small
when subject=school
shape tell
hook school_news
opens ask,share,tease
- There's a rumor going around class. Want to hear it?

@rule small.stranger.wary~state
on small
when rel=stranger
shape state
hook stranger_wary
opens ask,praise,share
- Oh. Hi. Yeah, it's... nice, I guess.
- Um, hello? Sure.
- Hello. Nice to meet you, I guess.
- Hi. I don't really know you yet.
- It's a little sudden. But hello.
- I think someone mentioned you. I'm not sure.
- I don't really talk to people I don't know. Don't take it badly.
- My friends are waiting, sort of. Just so you know.
- Well. Hi, I guess. Most people don't.
- Nice of you to say something. Thanks.

@rule small.stranger.who~q
on small
when rel=stranger
shape q
hook stranger_who
opens ask,share,tease
- Do I know you? Yeah, it's... nice, I guess.
- Hey. You're one of the new boys, right? I've seen you around.
- Oh, hi there. Can I help you?
- Um... hi? Did you need something?
- Oh! Hello. Do we have a class together?
- Sorry, I'm not used to this. Who are you, again?
- You sit near the back, right? I wondered who that was.
- Are you always this friendly? Okay.
- Do you say hi to everyone? Good to know.

@rule small.cool.flat~state
on small
when voice=cool|serious|proper
shape state
hook cool_flat
opens ask,agree,tease
- {Thing}. Hm. It's fine.
- If you insist. I have no strong opinion.
- Hm. {Thing}. I don't think about it much.
- That's a topic. It has its merits.
- Fine. I could take it or leave it.
- There are worse subjects than {thing}. Barely.
- I've read about {thing}. It was brief.
- I'd rather not waste words on {thing}. Yours may be different.
- I don't dislike it. That's the most I'll say.
- It serves its purpose. Next.

@rule small.cool.test~state
on small
when voice=cool|serious|proper
shape state
hook cool_test
opens ask,share,tease
- I suppose we can talk about {thing}. Go on.
- Most opinions on {thing} are noise. Prove me wrong.
- You're persistent, I'll give you that. Continue.
- Hm. You might know more than I do. I doubt it, though.

@rule small.cool.test~q
on small
when voice=cool|serious|proper
shape q
hook cool_test
opens ask,share,tease
- {Thing}? Unusual choice. What about it?
- You want my opinion on {thing}? It's adequate.
- Is this how you start every conversation? Interesting.
- You came here for {thing}? I see.

@rule small.shy.quiet~state
on small
when voice=shy|bookish
feel shy
shape state
hook shy_quiet
opens ask,praise,comfort
- Ah, {thing}... I... I like it, I think.
- U-um, {thing}? Sorry, I'm not good at this.
- Um... {thing}... I-I'll try.
- Um, {thing} is... nice? Please don't laugh.
- I-I think about it sometimes. That's all, sorry.
- Me? About {thing}? Um, okay.
- I wrote something about {thing} once. N-never mind.
- S-sorry, my voice got quiet. I can repeat it.
- I'm not used to talking this much. Thank you for listening.
- {Thing} is... um... good. I think.
- I don't know much, but {thing} seems nice. Sorry.
- You're really nice to talk to me about {thing}. Thanks.

@rule small.shy.ask~q
on small
when voice=shy|bookish
feel shy
shape q
hook shy_ask
opens ask,share,praise
- O-oh, you want to talk to me? I don't know what to say.
- Sorry, I get nervous. Is that a weird answer?
- Y-you're asking me? I'm not sure I'm the right person.
- I-I'd have to think... Can you wait?
- I-is it okay if I ask you too? What do you think?

@rule small.shy.quiet~q
on small
when voice=shy|bookish
feel shy
shape q
hook shy_quiet
opens ask,praise,comfort
- Ah... yes, {thing}. Do you?

# Pesos de implementação: em cada lugar, primeiro os valores que mudam o sentido da fala. Biblioteca: livros
# (l_study), silêncio, prova, depois chuva (wet), depois a briga na cabeça dela (fight/{fightwho}); as falas compostas
# (vários valores juntos) vencem sozinhas quando tudo vale, porque somam mais pontos. Chuva: weather
# (clear|cloudy|rain|storm), wet, rainlater, outside, rainlover. Gostos como chaves: l_study, l_food, l_animals...
# ---- your lines: the weather as it really is

@rule me.small.weather.rain
on me.small
when subject=weather wet=yes
- [Some rain, huh?|It's really coming down.|Did you bring an umbrella?]
- [I love the sound of rain on the windows.|Guess nobody's going outside today.|The whole university smells like rain.]
- [My shoes are still wet from this morning.|Think it'll stop before we go home?|Rainy days make everything slower, huh?]
- [Did you walk here in that?|How wet did you get this morning?]
- [I hope it stops soon.|I kind of hope it keeps going.] [You?|It's nice.]
- [The hallway smells like wet umbrellas.|Everyone's stuck indoors today.] [Hah.|Crowded, huh?]
- [It's been raining all day.|How long has it been raining?] [Think it'll end?|Feels like forever.]
- [Got a spare umbrella?|Do you need to share an umbrella later?]

@rule me.small.weather.storm
on me.small
when subject=weather weather=storm
- [Did you hear that thunder?|This storm is crazy.|The windows are shaking.]
- [Are you okay with thunder?|I think the power flickered.|Nobody's going home in this.]
- [Some storm, huh?|The wind's howling out there.|Glad we're inside.]
- [How are you getting home in this?|Do you think they'll stop the trains?]
- [That one was close.|Did you see that flash?] [You okay?|Wow.]
- [I'd stay away from the windows.|They should send everyone home.]
- [Does thunder bother you?|Stay inside for a while, okay?]
- [The rain's going sideways.|I've never seen it this bad.] [Look at that.|Scary, huh?]

@rule me.small.weather.later
on me.small
when subject=weather rainlater=yes
- [Looks like rain later.|The sky's getting dark.|Did you bring an umbrella? It's going to pour.]
- [Those clouds don't look friendly.|The forecast said rain this afternoon.|Feels like it's about to rain.]
- [Smells like rain.|The air's heavy today.|I give it an hour before it starts.]
- [You should head home before it starts.|Got your umbrella for later?]
- [It's getting darker over there.|That wind feels like rain.] [See?|You think so?]
- [I bet it starts right when class ends.|It'll hit just as we leave, watch.]
- [Are you walking home today?|Is your club still meeting if it rains?]
- [I left my umbrella at home, of course.|The weather app says two hours.] [Great.|We'll see.]

@rule me.small.weather.clear
on me.small
when subject=weather weather=clear
- [Perfect weather today.|Not a cloud in the sky.|Sunny days are the best.]
- [Great day to be outside, huh?|It's warm today.|The sun's out for real.]
- [It's so nice out.|Feels like a day off, doesn't it?|Look at that blue sky.]
- [You should eat outside today.|The roof must be great right now.]
- {student}[I couldn't focus in class with that sun.|Nobody wanted to be inside today.] [You too?|Right?]
- [I hope it stays like this for the weekend.|It's almost too nice.]
- [Good day for a walk home.|Want to take the long way later?]
- [Look how clear it is.|You can see the mountains today.] [Nice, right?|Look.]

# ---- her answer: rain, by who she is
@rule small.weather.rain.gentle.quiet
on small
when subject=weather wet=yes tone=gentle
feel smile
hook weather_rain_gentle_quiet
opens ask,share,comfort
- I like the rain, a little. I catch myself humming along. It feels like the whole university is whispering.
- The rain makes everything so quiet. I could hum along all day.
- It's nice, isn't it? The sound. It makes me sleepy, though...
- I watched the drops race down the window. Don't laugh.
- My favorite one lost. Silly, I know.
- Everything's a little softer when it rains. Don't you think?
- The hallway lights look warmer today. I like it.
- I hummed something to the sound of it. Quietly.
- It's a nice rhythm, isn't it? I won't sing, don't worry.

@rule small.weather.rain.gentle.strays
